.ec1-venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# `.coverage*`, not `.coverage`: coverage.py writes parallel-mode data files as
# `.coverage.<host>.<pid>.<rand>`, and a combine collision leaves `.coverage 2`,
# `.coverage 3`, … . The bare pattern matched none of those, so heavy-tier residue
# escaped the ignore rule and dirtied the working tree — which is precisely what the
# repository-clean gates (UCOS-RIB-001 GATE-12, CK-REG-DRIFT, G-15) read as drift.
# Widening the EXISTING rule; no new ignore mechanism is introduced.
.coverage*
coverage.xml

# UCOS-GOV-006 (GOV-005 §5.1/§6.8) — formally declare generated evidence and
# editor/office lock files as NON-ARTIFACTS bounded by version control. Generated
# evidence is deterministically re-derivable output (regenerated each run), not a
# registerable repository artifact; ~$ files are transient Office owner/lock temp
# files. Declaring them here makes the intent explicit and keeps eligibility a
# pure function of the tracked/un-ignored corpus for all future growth.
determinism-evidence/
~$*


# EPIC-UKDA (Universal Knowledge & Decision Architecture) — generated canonical
# knowledge store + handbooks. The single authored-once source of this knowledge is
# engine/knowledge/seed.py (tracked engineering code); the knowledge/ directory is
# deterministically re-derivable output (`ucos-knowledge init` / `ucos-knowledge
# docs`), i.e. a GENERATED ARTIFACT (GOV-005 §5.3) bounded by the ignore authority,
# never hand-registered. Regenerated each run; must never be tracked or seen as drift.
# Anchored with a leading slash so ONLY the repo-root store is ignored — the
# engine/knowledge/ source package and its tests remain tracked.
/knowledge/


# UAKOS-CLOSURE-002 — deterministic engine OUTPUT (GOV-005 §5.3, re-derivable). The
# authored sources (closure_engine.py / phase2_engine.py / phase3_engine.py + README /
# CHARTER / CONSOLIDATION-PLAN / PHASE-002-README / PHASE-INTERFACE-CONTRACT) remain
# tracked; the numbered reports and JSON state are regenerated each run (`make closure`
# / `make closure-phase2` / `make closure-phase3`) and must never be tracked or seen as
# drift. Mirrors the existing determinism-evidence/ and /knowledge/ generated-artifact policy.
00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/[0-9][0-9]-*.md
00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/closure.json
00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/phase2.json
00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/phase3.json

# P0-FINAL-CONVERGENCE-001 — RE-ADMISSION of AUTHORED determinations. The rule above is
# stated at the GENUS ([0-9][0-9]-*.md) so that any FUTURE engine output is bounded without
# a new rule. That breadth was correct for engine output and wrong for everything else: the
# three engines emit exactly 43 such files, the directory holds 67, and the 24-file remainder
# is AUTHORED — hand-written Phase-004/Finalization determinations that no producer emits.
# Measured, three independent ways:
#   * 0 of the 24 carry the "generated by `closure_engine.py`" provenance banner that
#     41 of the 43 engine outputs carry;
#   * no .py anywhere in the repository writes any of these 24 filenames;
#   * `git log --all` is EMPTY for every one of them — never tracked in any commit.
# The consequence was not cosmetic. `UCOS-URAT-001/urat-declaration.json` names two of them
# (56- and 62-) as declared exclusions, and `UAKOS-CLOSURE-008/assimilation.json`,
# `ACEE-000001/acee.json` and `UCOS-URAT-001/urat.json` cite twelve, so the ignore rule hid
# AUTHORED Repository Truth that TRACKED declarations depend on. A fresh clone could never
# resolve them, and `test_constitutional_convergence.py[urat]` failed with "exclusion path
# does not resolve" on every clean checkout while passing locally off stale residue.
# Authored Repository Truth is never bounded by the ignore authority (GOV-005 §5.1); only
# deterministically re-derivable OUTPUT is (§5.3). These 24 are re-admitted by name rather
# than by narrowing the genus, so the genus keeps bounding all future engine output.
!00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/02-AUTHORITATIVE-SOURCE-REGISTER.md
!00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/13-CONSTITUTIONAL-GAP-REGISTER.md
!00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/15-CLOSURE-EVIDENCE-REPORT.md
!00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/19-REPOSITORY-TRUTH-DETERMINATION.md
!00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/49-REPOSITORY-CLOSURE-PIPELINE-ARCHITECTURE.md
!00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/50-PIPELINE-GOVERNANCE-SPECIFICATION.md
!00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/51-PIPELINE-LIFECYCLE-INTEGRATION.md
!00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/52-REPOSITORY-ENTRY-POINT-SPECIFICATION.md
!00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/53-OPERATIONAL-EXECUTION-MODEL.md
!00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/54-REPOSITORY-CLOSURE-QUALITY-GATES.md
!00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/55-PIPELINE-EVOLUTION-STRATEGY.md
!00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/56-CONSTITUTIONAL-RATIFICATION-RECOMMENDATION.md
!00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/57-PHASE-004-DETERMINATION.md
!00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/58-PROGRAM-COMPLETENESS-ASSESSMENT.md
!00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/59-CONSTITUTIONAL-ALIGNMENT-ASSESSMENT.md
